---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import SectionHead from '~/components/SectionHead.astro'
import Logo from '~/components/Logo.astro'
import { REFERENCE_STATS, SITE } from '~/data/site'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Deployments"
  description="The OIML SMART AI reference instance running the Konneal engine in production, and how a deployment is white-labeled to the organization."
>
  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-12 pt-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-16">
      <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-sans text-[2.1rem] font-semibold leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.01em] sm:text-[2.7rem]">
        Deployments in production
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        The claims on this site are testable, because one deployment of the engine is public. It belongs to a real
        standards organization, serves its real corpus, and runs the same gates on every change that your deployment
        would run.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.2fr)_minmax(0,1fr)]">
        <div>
          <SectionHead
            title={SITE.reference.name}
            lede="The public question-answering service of the International Organization of Legal Metrology, running the Konneal engine in production — cited answers, computed verdicts, and the full measurement discipline, purely on open-weight models."
          />
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
            <a
              href={SITE.reference.url}
              class="border border-blue bg-blue px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.85rem] text-white transition-colors hover:bg-[#1c2f73]">
              {SITE.reference.url.replace('https://', '')} ↗
            </a>
            <a
              href={SITE.reference.howItWorksUrl}
              class="border border-rule bg-surface px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-[0.85rem] text-blue transition-colors hover:border-keyline">
              How it works, for its readers ↗
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
            The engine behind it — retrieval over clause-structured corpora, the answer contract, conformance by
            execution, the evaluation gates — is the same package every deployment consumes, promoted through the same
            golden suites that grade the live service.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col justify-center gap-8 border border-rule bg-surface p-8">
          <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-6 font-mono text-[0.78rem]">
            {
              REFERENCE_STATS.map(([label, value]) => (
                <div>
                  <dt class="text-ink-faint">{label}</dt>
                  <dd class="text-[1.3rem] font-medium text-blue">{value}</dd>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-rule">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
        <div>
          <SectionHead
            title="White-labeled to your organization"
            lede="A deployment carries your publications, your terminology, your profile and your frontend. Konneal appears only in a small credit beside your emblem."
          />
          <p class="mt-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            The credit lockup is specified in the brand: “Powered by” set in the regular weight at reduced ink, the
            mark at 1.4 × the wordmark’s x-height, baseline-aligned. It sits beside institutional emblems, not above
            them.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center border border-rule bg-surface p-12">
          <Logo variant="light" lockup="credit" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8">
      <div class="border border-blue/25 bg-surface p-8">
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[0.98rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Adoption follows what your organization already has: a Metanorma library is enough to begin, and every
          further asset raises the annealment your members get.
        </p>
        <a href="/get-started/" class="mt-6 inline-block font-mono text-[0.8rem] text-blue hover:text-keyline">
          The adoption paths → Get started
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
